response:
If I could invite anyone in history to a dinner party and have a chat with them, I'd choose Aristotle, Marie Curie, Zheng He, Edgar Allan Poe, and Albert Einstein.

Aristotle would be there to discuss philosophy and logic with, as he's the founding father of many western philosophical streams;
Marie Curie would represent the spirit of human perseverance and scientific pursuit;
Zheng He would tell the tales of his great voyages which were far more magnificent than any stories told in history books;
Edgar Allan Poe would provide some gothic romantic poetry to liven up the place;
And lastly, Albert Einstein would explain to everyone what exactly is relativity and how it changed our understanding of the universe!

This group would make every topic of conversation an unforgettable experience, whether it be about the past, present or future!

If I were to host an imaginative dinner party with historical figures, I would make sure to have a mix of thinkers, leaders, and creators across different domains so we could all exchange ideas and have interesting conversation starters. The guests would be:

1. Marie Curie - one of the greatest physicists and chemists in human history; 
2. Leonardo Da Vinci - a genius artist and inventor who had thoughts way ahead of his time;
3. Alexander the Great - a military genius who shaped ancient history;
4. Marie Antoinette - a French queen with an incredibly influential lifestyle at the peak of French culture; 
5. Albert Einstein - probably the most famous scientist humanity has ever seen;
6. Ada Lovelace - a British mathematician that was ultra modern for her era;
7. Joan of Arc - a national heroine of France with extremely inspiring life stories.

This eclectic mix of guests would definitely give everyone quite a few topics to discuss about science, culture, military, lifestyle, philosophy, math, and humanities. This would be an epic dinner indeed!
